th respect to $u$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\int \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=- \\frac{\\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{4}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{\\cos{\\left(4 x + 3 \\right)}}{4}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678094 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d0f4e21-6b1a-544d-9189-ecf9b2f0cc03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678085}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d0f4e21-6b1a-544d-9189-ecf9b2f0cc03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678085} :answer-field/id #uuid "559a1b3d-66d6-54fa-b0b3-ca7a3aa0bb64" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678067}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9891ad60-b02c-519b-bb3b-3ccdc5f192ce" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\cos{\\left(\\pi - 3 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\sin{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\sin{\\left(\\pi \\right)}=0,\\quad \\sin{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}=1$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\pi - 3 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-3.\n$$\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=\\pi\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{6}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe new bounds decrease. Keep this order when evaluating the antiderivative.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\cos{\\left(\\pi - 3 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\int_{\\pi}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\left[- \\frac{\\sin{\\left(u \\right)}}{3}\\right]_{\\pi}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}=\\left(- \\frac{1}{3}\\right)-\\left(0\\right).\n$$\n\nThe answer is\n\n$$\n- \\frac{1}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678113 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "174e1f57-27ba-5b50-8e1c-98e49800fec6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}} \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678045} {:answer/id #uuid "2d555d93-51bc-5e73-a1f2-f1cf1d9857aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi} \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678051} {:answer/id #uuid "3b4ee5ed-af33-5a5b-815c-d2c4ac4b12e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\left(\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi} \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678060} {:answer/id #uuid "7ecfbe3a-e6bb-54c2-bc5a-e26384ccaeb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi} \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678086} {:answer/id #uuid "de064156-605e-5acc-9433-8f67797fd421" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\int_{2 \\pi}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}} \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678120}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d555d93-51bc-5e73-a1f2-f1cf1d9857aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi} \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678051} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae68e617-0d18-59ff-b276-92bb3877ffb1" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678105}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cc8aa811-99e1-5f7b-aa43-885740447191" :question/problem "Use the substitution $u=3 x$. Which integral is obtained?\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}} \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=3 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}\\\\x=\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}&\\Longrightarrow u=2 \\pi\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}} \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi} \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformed integral is\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi} \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678115 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74c24471-9d9e-52c9-9422-32e366c0f2a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678080}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74c24471-9d9e-52c9-9422-32e366c0f2a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678080} :answer-field/id #uuid "334999f2-0ee1-5d2c-a8b2-9f1cd538e034" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678056}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cce7215f-f09f-5bb0-8216-21c5515d0db7" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} 4 \\sin{\\left(- 3 x + 2 \\pi \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=- \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\cos{\\left(2 \\pi \\right)}=1,\\quad \\cos{\\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{2} \\right)}=0$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=- 3 x + 2 \\pi$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-3.\n$$\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=2 \\pi\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{6}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe new bounds decrease. Keep this order when evaluating the antiderivative.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} 4 \\sin{\\left(- 3 x + 2 \\pi \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{4}{3}\\left(\\int_{2 \\pi}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}} \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\frac{4 \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{3}\\right]_{2 \\pi}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}=\\left(0\\right)-\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right).\n$$\n\nThe answer is\n\n$$\n- \\frac{4}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678122 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5871b02d-2bef-5fb1-865e-65aff4cc3969" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678068}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5871b02d-2bef-5fb1-865e-65aff4cc3969" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678068} :answer-field/id #uuid "866f3cb3-d08c-55fc-9741-2055767f7e3a" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678091}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e448a4d2-65fb-5da5-83af-e67ab30b203d" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{8}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} 3 \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\sin{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\sin{\\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{2} \\right)}=-1,\\quad \\sin{\\left(2 \\pi \\right)}=0$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=4 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=4.\n$$\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{3 \\pi}{8}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=2 \\pi\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{8}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} 3 \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{3}{4}\\left(\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi} \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\frac{3 \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}}{4}\\right]_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi}=\\left(0\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{3}{4}\\right).\n$$\n\nThe answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678123 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8bb3a90-6824-5d37-96be-dd04dbd40003" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\sin{\\left(1 - 2 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678101}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8bb3a90-6824-5d37-96be-dd04dbd40003" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\sin{\\left(1 - 2 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678101} :answer-field/id #uuid "44f876a5-6b10-5536-9bb9-84048b43931d" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678061}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e7ec123b-4f1a-58be-a8aa-4b6e169ef8a2" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int 2 \\cos{\\left(1 - 2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\sin{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\n{{answer}} $+C$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=1 - 2 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-2.\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 2 \\cos{\\left(1 - 2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=-\\left(\\int \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate with respect to $u$:\n\n$$\n-\\left(\\int \\cos{\\