uestion/worked-solution "Let $u=3 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\int \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformed integral is\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\int \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678128 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d59fc83-7aa0-595d-aed1-8be7cb662f5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678070}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d59fc83-7aa0-595d-aed1-8be7cb662f5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678070} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f4984fe-084f-51a5-bb0d-e7dc322c9849" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678087}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ee47bd77-b3fc-5c96-b3c1-1120ca3a9273" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} \\sin{\\left(\\pi - 4 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=- \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\cos{\\left(\\pi \\right)}=-1,\\quad \\cos{\\left(0 \\right)}=1$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\pi - 4 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-4.\n$$\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=\\pi\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe new bounds decrease. Keep this order when evaluating the antiderivative.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} \\sin{\\left(\\pi - 4 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\int_{\\pi}^{0} \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\frac{\\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{4}\\right]_{\\pi}^{0}=\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{1}{4}\\right).\n$$\n\nThe answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678130 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21ace9e0-6bda-5c7f-ac52-9b7bae7dcbe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21ace9e0-6bda-5c7f-ac52-9b7bae7dcbe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678047} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc9a28eb-7848-5087-9875-b8382c66378c" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678114}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f85dd1a8-9614-5c1d-8fde-7f1192c68aed" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} 3 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=- \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\cos{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}=0,\\quad \\cos{\\left(\\pi \\right)}=-1$.\n\n{{answer}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\pi\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} 3 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi} \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\left[- \\frac{3 \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{2}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}=\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)-\\left(0\\right).\n$$\n\nThe answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678132 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12e05b3a-ae3e-5532-aa5e-3bf110c781f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\left(\\int_{\\pi}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}} \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678041} {:answer/id #uuid "6c755fac-f0bb-5269-979c-07c4aa6a8b15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\left(\\int_{\\pi}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}} \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678075} {:answer/id #uuid "ad9cf26a-eeb8-5ee6-8b56-ffd488817d72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\pi}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}} \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678104} {:answer/id #uuid "ed67b1e6-bb5d-5999-98d5-613c2c5849e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{\\pi} \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678127} {:answer/id #uuid "eff62eea-eadd-56a5-bc38-0c50f5ee20f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}} \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678129}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad9cf26a-eeb8-5ee6-8b56-ffd488817d72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\pi}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}} \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678104} :answer-field/id #uuid "0508bed8-6f0c-5744-9d06-ee9974f77066" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678034}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fdf6518e-e8a4-59f1-9024-2dc25c55475a" :question/problem "Use the substitution $u=2 x$. Which integral is obtained?\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}} 2 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\pi\\\\x=\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}} 2 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int_{\\pi}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}} \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformed integral is\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\pi}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}} \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682475 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "449e0e1d-9a6c-5fe1-a95b-b639f4ccd423" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\cos{\\left(2 x + 1 \\right)}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682488}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "449e0e1d-9a6c-5fe1-a95b-b639f4ccd423" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\cos{\\left(2 x + 1 \\right)}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682488} :answer-field/id #uuid "63f21da6-ff1f-5651-915c-74c67a35db91" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682490}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0b089ae1-11ab-5fa6-bab3-121d25262e59" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int 3 \\sin{\\left(2 x + 1 \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}} $+C$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2 x + 1$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 3 \\sin{\\left(2 x + 1 \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\int \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=- \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nIntegrate with respect to $u$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\int \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=- \\frac{3 \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{3 \\cos{\\left(2 x + 1 \\right)}}{2}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682479 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0901d33-2e89-5f39-add8-8a70956d5f7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682515}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0901d33-2e89-5f39-add8-8a70956d5f7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682515} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d3edd1e-c3e5-5543-a37f-9d5e1955e37c" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682495}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "196fe2f7-2cc5-56b3-b0b3-c2bc0194f4ca" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\cos{\\left(\\pi - 3 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\pi - 3 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-3.\n$$\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=\\pi\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{6}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe new bounds decrease. Keep this order when evaluating the antiderivative.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\cos{\\left(\\pi - 3 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\int_{\\pi}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\sin{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\sin{\\left(\\pi \\right)}=0,\\quad \\sin{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}=1$.\n\nIntegrate and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\left[- \\frac{\\sin{\\left(u \\right)}}{3}\\right]_{\\pi}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}=\\left(- \\frac{1}{3}\\right)-\\left(0\\right).\n$$\n\nThe answer is\n\n$$\n- \\frac{1}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682481 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "caed2feb-8122-5cc5-b89b-a8b6595154f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "caed2feb-8122-5cc5-b89b-a8b6595154f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682510} :answer-field/id #uuid "9aa79387-ab64-5460-8503-123d889a9347" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682502}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "25017208-d35a-5987-9f5a-ab92bf702b0c" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} 4 \\sin{\\left(- 3 x + 2 \\pi \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=- 3 x + 2 \\pi$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-3.\n$$\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=2 \\pi\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{6}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe new bounds decrease. Keep this order when evaluating the antiderivative.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} 4 \\sin{\\left(- 3 x + 2 \\pi \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{4}{3}\\left(\\int_{2 \\pi}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}} \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=- \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\cos{\\left(2 \\pi \\right)}=1,\\quad \\cos{\\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{2} \\right)}=0$.\n\nIntegrate and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\frac{4 \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{3}\\right]_{2 \\pi}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}=\\left(0\\right)-\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right).\n$$\n\nThe answer is\n\n$$\n- \\frac{4}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682484 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db631def-0fa3-54f6-a633-156d28801a11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db631def-0fa3-54f6-a633-156d28801a11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682514} :answer-field/id #uuid "d26e671a-fc5b-5cf6-9ef2-b441436e52ed" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682511}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2f366558-9e7a-541a-91d0-27b02256448d" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} 2 \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=3 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{\\pi}{3}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\pi\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} 2 \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\int_{\\pi}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}} \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\sin{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\sin{\\left(\\pi \\right)}=0,\\quad \\sin{\\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{2} \\right)}=-1$.\n\nIntegrate and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\frac{2 \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}}{3}\\right]_{\\pi}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}=\\left(- \\frac{2}{3}\\right)-\\left(0\\right).\n$$\n\nThe answer is\n\n$$\n- \\frac{2}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682486 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7dac586-8937-596c-a536-0affac3403ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\cos{\\left(4 x + 3 \\right)}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682518}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7dac586-8937-596c-a536-0affac3403ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\cos{\\left(4 x + 3 \\right)}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682518} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4725154-97d7-5a06-956a-ad97366aaa54" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682520}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3fa4f0a8-a5a5-599b-b592-922d02da7a32" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\sin{\\left(4 x + 3 \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}} $+C$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=4 x + 3$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=4.\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\sin{\\left(4 x + 3 \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\int \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=- \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nIntegrate with respect to $u$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\int \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=- \\frac{\\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{4}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{\\cos{\\left(4 x + 3 \\right)}}{4}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682487 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d28d9e19-507c-508e-8f85-ad58d778e94b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682512}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d28d9e19-507c-508e-8f85-ad58d778e94b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682512} :answer-field/id #uuid "226db927-2cc9-5970-ac75-31697172e7bc" :