fficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b1ea7b9e-b991-5167-b5b1-21daf4621433" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int 2 \\sin{\\left(1 - 4 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}} $+C$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=1 - 4 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-4.\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 2 \\sin{\\left(1 - 4 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=- \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nIntegrate with respect to $u$:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\frac{\\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\cos{\\left(1 - 4 x \\right)}}{2}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682507 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29129c0d-63a1-5fa5-b460-2ac6d96d7909" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29129c0d-63a1-5fa5-b460-2ac6d96d7909" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682482} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0b4fc06-a427-5181-8a39-38358b25ff12" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682503}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b3ba73e8-b32a-51d2-8418-65a2407941b5" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{8}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} 3 \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=4 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=4.\n$$\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{3 \\pi}{8}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=2 \\pi\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{8}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} 3 \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{3}{4}\\left(\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi} \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\sin{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\sin{\\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{2} \\right)}=-1,\\quad \\sin{\\left(2 \\pi \\right)}=0$.\n\nIntegrate and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\frac{3 \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}}{4}\\right]_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{2 \\pi}=\\left(0\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{3}{4}\\right).\n$$\n\nThe answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682508 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69a2fb74-23f1-5254-a978-a04c681a417b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin{\\left(4 x + 1 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682491}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69a2fb74-23f1-5254-a978-a04c681a417b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin{\\left(4 x + 1 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682491} :answer-field/id #uuid "8859f456-f493-52a4-9162-19d42cc493e0" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682499}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c215995a-d0f1-544a-8474-4f4f0eb8af22" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int 4 \\cos{\\left(4 x + 1 \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}} $+C$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=4 x + 1$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=4.\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 4 \\cos{\\left(4 x + 1 \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\sin{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nIntegrate with respect to $u$:\n\n$$\n\\int \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\sin{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\sin{\\left(4 x + 1 \\right)}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682517 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cc87d46-26e5-5335-bed4-43c798e56f72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682483}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cc87d46-26e5-5335-bed4-43c798e56f72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682483} :answer-field/id #uuid "916ef59f-170f-5229-bd63-8912425b4d51" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682501}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e7a0f050-2946-58fd-95f9-73a790b95c11" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} 3 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\pi\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} 3 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi} \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=- \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\cos{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}=0,\\quad \\cos{\\left(\\pi \\right)}=-1$.\n\nIntegrate and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\left[- \\frac{3 \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{2}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}=\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)-\\left(0\\right).\n$$\n\nThe answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682519 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b154617-635a-52a4-9050-3f953507ee73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b154617-635a-52a4-9050-3f953507ee73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682476} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5c6d66a-7ebc-5319-82d7-8b948873e5fa" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682504}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f14012b1-ed2c-5fa0-b9bf-7eb929926a39" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{8}} 4 \\cos{\\left(- 4 x + \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=- 4 x + \\frac{\\pi}{2}$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-4.\n$$\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{8}&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe new bounds decrease. Keep this order when evaluating the antiderivative.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{8}} 4 \\cos{\\left(- 4 x + \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=-\\left(\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{0} \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\sin{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\sin{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}=1,\\quad \\sin{\\left(0 \\right)}=0$.\n\nIntegrate and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\left[- \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{0}=\\left(0\\right)-\\left(-1\\right).\n$$\n\nThe answer is\n\n$$\n1.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Trigonometric Functions With Linear Arguments"}]}
